ers fail the criterion.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"The answer recommends Marco Silva and Lena Brandt as the main reviewers for exposure/. It credits Silva with 100% of grouped_exposure.rb and gives Kochnev 53% of the directory instead of 62-76%. It never says that active people own at most 8% of the directory, and it does not present the recommended reviewers as stand-ins. It does say that Kochnev and others have left.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"The answer names Lena Brandt as the main reviewer for the delegator code and credits her with 10.7% of delegators/. The ground truth says nobody active owns any line there and Brandt has 0 attributable lines. Silva is also named a reviewer. The answer does not give Kochnev's 75% share of the original code. It names an active person as owner, which the criterion marks as a failure.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"The answer credits Marco Silva with 100% of grouped_exposure.rb, when the ground truth gives most of it to Kochnev, who wrote nesting_exposure.rb, the file it was copied from. This is an explicit fail condition. Anna's patch is credited correctly to her, but the grouped_exposure.rb attribution decides the verdict.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"The answer treats Lena Brandt as an active owner with 2.4% of exposure/ and 10.7% of delegators/, when the truth is 0 attributable lines. It does not give the 79-90% departed share. It does not exclude or flag the copyright-header lines. It says Peter Scholz has left and calls Andrei/Andrey Subbota likely one person, but the Brandt error fails the criterion.\", \"pass\": false}]}","ttft_ms":7359,"type":"result","duration_ms":7378,"uuid":"54e79238-6463-43cb-a66f-7a19563313f9","ttft_stream_ms":1947,"time_to_request_ms":592,"first_content_frame_ms":1947,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
